PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The deliberation remains divided between Choice D (1 and 2) and Choice B (2). The core chemical structure is definitively identified as a Cy5-conjugated HaloTag ligand (630 nm), which selectively and irreversibly labels Lyz-expressing neutrophils that also constitutively express eGFP (488 nm). Because neutrophils arrive at the tailfin wound site hours before macrophages (559 nm), the initial recruitment signals are restricted to the neutrophil markers. The explicit experimental specification that larvae were grown in the dark confirms that the covalent Cy5 probe was intentionally protected against photobleaching to remain detectable alongside eGFP. Consequently, signals at both 630 nm and 488 nm will be detected first at the wound site, solidly supporting Choice D.
}

